>
<hr data-start=3D"832" data-end=3D"835" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"837" data-end=3D"898" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"83=
9" data-end=3D"898">Chapitre 1 : Introduction aux Signaux (Niveau D=C3=A9bu=
tant)</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"900" data-end=3D"935" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"90=
3" data-end=3D"935">1.1 Qu'est-ce qu'un Signal ?</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"1237" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=3D=
"940" data-end=3D"950">signal</strong> est une variation de grandeurs physi=
ques (comme la tension, l'intensit=C3=A9 lumineuse, ou la fr=C3=A9quence) q=
ui permet de transporter des informations d'un endroit =C3=A0 un autre. Les=
 signaux peuvent =C3=AAtre de nature <strong data-start=3D"1154" data-end=
=3D"1168">analogique</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"1172" data-end=3D"11=
85">num=C3=A9rique</strong>, selon la fa=C3=A7on dont l'information est rep=
r=C3=A9sent=C3=A9e.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1269" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1243" data-end=3D"1269">1.1.1 Types de Signaux</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1270" data-end=3D"1737">
<li data-start=3D"1270" data-end=3D"1475" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1272" data-end=3D"1475" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
272" data-end=3D"1293">Signal Analogique</strong> : Un signal analogique es=
t une repr=C3=A9sentation continue de l'information, qui varie de mani=C3=
=A8re fluide, sans sauts. Exemples : la variation de la temp=C3=A9rature, l=
=E2=80=99intensit=C3=A9 sonore, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1476" data-end=3D"1737" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1478" data-end=3D"1737" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
478" data-end=3D"1498">Signal Num=C3=A9rique</strong> : Un signal num=C3=A9=
rique, quant =C3=A0 lui, est discret, c'est-=C3=A0-dire qu'il prend des val=
eurs distinctes, g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement sous forme de bits (0 et 1). Exempl=
es : les donn=C3=A9es binaires utilis=C3=A9es dans les ordinateurs, les t=
=C3=A9l=C3=A9communications num=C3=A9riques.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start=3D"1739" data-end=3D"1781" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1742" data-end=3D"1781">1.2 Pourquoi Utiliser des Signaux ?</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1782" data-end=3D"1871" class=3D"">Les signaux sont utilis=
=C3=A9s pour transmettre des informations sur des distances variables :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1872" data-end=3D"2162">
<li data-start=3D"1872" data-end=3D"2033" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1874" data-end=3D"2033" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
874" data-end=3D"1897">Signaux analogiques</strong> : utilis=C3=A9s dans de=
s applications comme la radio, la t=C3=A9l=C3=A9vision traditionnelle, et l=
a transmission de voix via les lignes t=C3=A9l=C3=A9phoniques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2034" data-end=3D"2162" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2036" data-end=3D"2162" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
036" data-end=3D"2058">Signaux num=C3=A9riques</strong> : utilis=C3=A9s dan=
s les ordinateurs, les r=C3=A9seaux, le traitement de donn=C3=A9es, et les =
communications modernes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2164" data-end=3D"2167" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"2169" data-end=3D"2241" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2171" data-end=3D"2241">Chapitre 2 : Signaux Analogiques (Niveau D=C3=A9but=
ant =C3=A0 Interm=C3=A9diaire)</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"2243" data-end=3D"2289" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2246" data-end=3D"2289">2.1 Qu'est-ce qu'un Signal Analogique ?</strong></h=
2>
<p data-start=3D"2291" data-end=3D"2567" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"2294" data-end=3D"2315">signal analogique</strong> est une repr=C3=A9se=
ntation continue de l=E2=80=99information, ce qui signifie qu=E2=80=99il pe=
ut prendre une infinit=C3=A9 de valeurs dans une plage donn=C3=A9e. Les sig=
naux analogiques sont souvent associ=C3=A9s =C3=A0 des ph=C3=A9nom=C3=A8nes=
 naturels, tels que le son, la lumi=C3=A8re ou la temp=C3=A9rature.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2569" data-end=3D"2623" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2573" data-end=3D"2623">2.1.1 Caract=C3=A9ristiques des Signaux Analogiques=
</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"3124">
<li data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2844" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2626" data-end=3D"2844" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
626" data-end=3D"2639">Amplitude</strong> : L'amplitude d'un signal analogi=
que correspond =C3=A0 la hauteur de la variation du signal (par exemple, le=
 volume sonore). L'amplitude peut =C3=AAtre mesur=C3=A9e en volts, d=C3=A9c=
ibels, ou autres unit=C3=A9s selon le domaine.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2845" data-end=3D"3041" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2847" data-end=3D"3041" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
847" data-end=3D"2860">Fr=C3=A9quence</strong> : La fr=C3=A9quence mesure l=
e nombre de fois que le signal oscille par seconde (en Hertz - Hz). Par exe=
mple, une fr=C3=A9quence de 1 kHz signifie que le signal oscille 1000 fois =
par seconde.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3042" data-end=3D"3124" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3044" data-end=3D"3124" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
044" data-end=3D"3053">Phase</strong> : La phase indique le d=C3=A9calage t=
emporel entre deux signaux oscillants.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3126" data-end=3D"3171" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3130" data-end=3D"3171">2.1.2 Exemples de Signaux Analogiques</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3172" data-end=3D"3411">
<li data-start=3D"3172" data-end=3D"3283" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3174" data-end=3D"3283" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
174" data-end=3D"3190">Signal Audio</strong> : Un microphone convertit les =
sons (vibrations de l'air) en un signal =C3=A9lectrique analogique.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3284" data-end=3D"3411" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3286" data-end=3D"3411" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
286" data-end=3D"3302">Signal Vid=C3=A9o</strong> : Les anciennes transmiss=
ions de t=C3=A9l=C3=A9vision utilisaient des signaux analogiques pour trans=
mettre les images.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3413" data-end=3D"3477" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3417" data-end=3D"3477">2.1.3 Avantages et Inconv=C3=A9nients des Signaux A=
nalogiques</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3478" data-end=3D"3809">
<li data-start=3D"3478" data-end=3D"3649" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3480" data-end=3D"3496" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
480" data-end=3D"3493">Avantages</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3499" data-end=3D"3649">
<li data-start=3D"3499" data-end=3D"3608" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3501" data-end=3D"3608" class=3D"">Repr=C3=A9sentation con=
tinue, ce qui permet des transmissions fluides et pr=C3=A9cises dans des sy=
st=C3=A8mes analogiques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3611" data-end=3D"3649" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3613" data-end=3D"3649" class=3D"">Tr=C3=A8s adapt=C3=A9 a=
ux ph=C3=A9nom=C3=A8nes naturels.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3650" data-end=3D"3809" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3652" data-end=3D"3671" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
652" data-end=3D"3669">Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3674" data-end=3D"3809">
<li data-start=3D"3674" data-end=3D"3716" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3676" data-end=3D"3716" class=3D"">Sensibles aux interf=C3=
=A9rences et au bruit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3719" data-end=3D"3809" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3721" data-end=3D"3809" class=3D"">Difficiles =C3=A0 trait=
er sur de longues distances sans amplification et nettoyage du signal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3811" data-end=3D"3814" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3816" data-end=3D"3877" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3819" data-end=3D"3877">2.2 Conversion Analogique : Modulation et D=C3=A9mo=
dulation</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3879" data-end=3D"3914" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3883" data-end=3D"3914">2.2.1 Modulation Analogique</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3915" data-end=3D"4133" class=3D"">La <strong data-start=
=3D"3918" data-end=3D"3932">modulation</strong> est un proc=C3=A9d=C3=A9 ut=
ilis=C3=A9 pour modifier un signal porteur (g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement une onde=
 porteuse de haute fr=C3=A9quence) avec un signal d'information analogique.=
 Les principaux types de modulation analogique sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4134" data-end=3D"4450">
<li data-start=3D"4134" data-end=3D"4245" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4136" data-end=3D"4245" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
136" data-end=3D"4167">Modulation d'Amplitude (AM)</strong> : La variation =
de l'amplitude du signal porteuse repr=C3=A9sente les informations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4246" data-end=3D"4350" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4248" data-end=3D"4350" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
248" data-end=3D"4280">Modulation de Fr=C3=A9quence (FM)</strong> : La fr=
=C3=A9quence du signal porteuse varie en fonction de l=E2=80=99information.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4351" data-end=3D"4450" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4353" data-end=3D"4450" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
353" data-end=3D"4381">Modulation de Phase (PM)</strong> : La phase de la p=
orteuse varie en fonction du signal d=E2=80=99information.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4452" data-end=3D"4478" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4456" data-end=3D"4478">2.2.2 D=C3=A9modulation</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4479" data-end=3D"4601" class=3D"">La <strong data-start=
=3D"4482" data-end=3D"4498">d=C3=A9modulation</strong> consiste =C3=A0 extr=
aire l=E2=80=99information du signal modul=C3=A9 =C3=A0 l'aide de technique=
s de filtrage et de d=C3=A9tection.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4603" data-end=3D"4606" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"4608" data-end=3D"4679" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4610" data-end=3D"4679">Chapitre 3 : Signaux Num=C3=A9riques (Niveau D=C3=
=A9butant =C3=A0 Interm=C3=A9diaire)</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"4681" data-end=3D"4726" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4684" data-end=3D"4726">3.1 Qu'est-ce qu'un Signal Num=C3=A9rique ?</strong=
></h2>
<p data-start=3D"4728" data-end=3D"5089" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"4731" data-end=3D"4751">signal num=C3=A9rique</strong> est une repr=C3=
=A9sentation discr=C3=A8te de l=E2=80=99information. Contrairement au signa=
l analogique, un signal num=C3=A9rique ne prend que des valeurs pr=C3=A9cis=
es =C3=A0 des moments d=C3=A9finis (g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement 0 ou 1 dans un s=
yst=C3=A8me binaire). Ces signaux sont utilis=C3=A9s dans la majorit=C3=A9 =
des technologies modernes, y compris les ordinateurs et les r=C3=A9seaux de=
 communication.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5091" data-end=3D"5144" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5095" data-end=3D"5144">3.1.1 Caract=C3=A9ristiques des Signaux Num=C3=A9ri=
ques</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5145" data-end=3D"5779">
<li data-start=3D"5145" data-end=3D"5324" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5147" data-end=3D"5324" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
147" data-end=3D"5164">Bits et Bytes</strong> : Un signal num=C3=A9rique es=
t constitu=C3=A9 de <strong data-start=3D"5204" data-end=3D"5212">bits</str=
ong> (0 et 1), qui sont regroup=C3=A9s pour former des <strong data-start=
=3D"5258" data-end=3D"5268">octets</strong> (bytes). Chaque bit repr=C3=A9s=
ente une unit=C3=A9 d'information.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5325" data-end=3D"5568" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5327" data-end=3D"5568" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
327" data-end=3D"5358">Fr=C3=A9quence d'=C3=A9chantillonnage</strong> : Le =
signal num=C3=A9rique est cr=C3=A9=C3=A9 en <strong data-start=3D"5393" dat=
a-end=3D"5412">=C3=A9chantillonnant</strong> un signal analogique =C3=A0 in=
tervalles r=C3=A9guliers, et la fr=C3=A9quence d=E2=80=99=C3=A9chantillonna=
ge d=C3=A9termine la pr=C3=A9cision de la repr=C3=A9sentation num=C3=A9riqu=
e du signal analogique.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5569" data-end=3D"5779" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5571" data-end=3D"5779" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
571" data-end=3D"5592">Niveaux de signal</strong> : Un signal num=C3=A9riqu=
e prend typiquement deux valeurs discr=C3=A8tes, par exemple 0 et 1. Ces va=
leurs sont repr=C3=A9sent=C3=A9es sous forme de tensions distinctes (par ex=
emple, 0V pour 0 et 5V pour 1).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5781" data-end=3D"5825" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5785" data-end=3D"5825">3.1.2 Exemples de Signaux Num=C3=A9riques</strong><=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5826" data-end=3D"6107">
<li data-start=3D"5826" data-end=3D"5980" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5828" data-end=3D"5980" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
828" data-end=3D"5869">Transmission de donn=C3=A9es informatiques</strong> =
: Les ordinateurs utilisent des signaux num=C3=A9riques pour transmettre de=
s donn=C3=A9es sur des r=C3=A9seaux informatiques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5981" data-end=3D"6107" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5983" data-end=3D"6107" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
983" data-end=3D"6011">Communication cellulaire</strong> : Les appels et me=
ssages SMS sont des exemples de signaux num=C3=A9riques dans les syst=C3=A8=
mes mobiles.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6109" data-end=3D"6172" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6113" data-end=3D"6172">3.1.3 Avantages et Inconv=C3=A9nients des Signaux N=
um=C3=A9riques</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6173" data-end=3D"6637">
<li data-start=3D"6173" data-end=3D"6377" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6175" data-end=3D"6190" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
175" data-end=3D"6188">Avantages</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6193" data-end=3D"6377">
<li data-start=3D"6193" data-end=3D"6241" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6195" data-end=3D"6241" class=3D"">Moins sensibles aux int=
erf=C3=A9rences et au bruit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6244" data-end=3D"6317" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6246" data-end=3D"6317" class=3D"">Facile =C3=A0 manipuler=
, stocker et traiter avec des syst=C3=A8mes informatiques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6320" data-end=3D"6377" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6322" data-end=3D"6377" class=3D"">Meilleure int=C3=A9grit=
=C3=A9 du signal sur de longues distances.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6378" data-end=3D"6637" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6380" data-end=3D"6399" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
380" data-end=3D"6397">Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6402" data-end=3D"6637">
<li data-start=3D"6402" data-end=3D"6539" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6404" data-end=3D"6539" class=3D"">Repr=C3=A9sentation dis=
cr=C3=A8te des informations, ce qui peut entra=C3=AEner des erreurs si l'=
=C3=A9chantillonnage ou la quantification est mal effectu=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6542" data-end=3D"6637" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6544" data-end=3D"6637" class=3D"">Peut n=C3=A9cessiter un=
 traitement plus complexe pour la conversion entre analogique et num=C3=A9r=
ique.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6639" data-end=3D"6642" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6644" data-end=3D"6696" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6647" data-end=3D"6696">3.2 Conversion Num=C3=A9rique : Codage et D=C3=A9co=
dage</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6698" data-end=3D"6718" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6702" data-end=3D"6718">3.2.1 Codage</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6719" data-end=3D"6993" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"6722" data-end=3D"6732">codage</strong> est le processus de conversion =
de l'information analogique en une forme num=C3=A9rique. Cela est g=C3=A9n=
=C3=A9ralement r=C3=A9alis=C3=A9 par un <strong data-start=3D"6853" data-en=
d=3D"6904">convertisseur analogique-num=C3=A9rique (CAN ou ADC)</strong>, q=
ui =C3=A9chantillonne et quantifie le signal analogique en une s=C3=A9rie d=
e valeurs num=C3=A9riques.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6995" data-end=3D"7017" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6999" data-end=3D"7017">3.2.2 D=C3=A9codage</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"7018" data-end=3D"7209" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"7021" data-end=3D"7033">d=C3=A9codage</strong> est le processus inverse=
, qui consiste =C3=A0 convertir un signal num=C3=A9rique en un signal analo=
gique. Cela se fait =C3=A0 l'aide d'un <strong data-start=3D"7157" data-end=
=3D"7208">convertisseur num=C3=A9rique-analogique (CNA ou DAC)</strong>.</p=
>
<hr data-start=3D"7211" data-end=3D"7214" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"7216" data-end=3D"7318" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7218" data-end=3D"7318">Chapitre 4 : Diff=C3=A9rences entre Signaux Analogi=
ques et Num=C3=A9riques (Niveau Interm=C3=A9diaire =C3=A0 Avanc=C3=A9)</str=
ong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"7320" data-end=3D"7380" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7323" data-end=3D"7380">4.1 Comparaison des Signaux Analogiques et Num=C3=
=A9riques</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7382" data-end=3D"7410" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7386" data-end=3D"7410">4.1.1 Repr=C3=A9sentation</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7411" data-end=3D"7590">
<li data-start=3D"7411" data-end=3D"7504" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7413" data-end=3D"7504" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
413" data-end=3D"7427">Analogique</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sentation continue, =
capable de transmettre des informations infinies.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7505" data-end=3D"7590" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7507" data-end=3D"7590" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
507" data-end=3D"7520">Num=C3=A9rique</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sentation discr=
=C3=A8te avec des valeurs limit=C3=A9es (souvent 0 et 1).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7592" data-end=3D"7615" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7596" data-end=3D"7615">4.1.2 Pr=C3=A9cision</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7616" data-end=3D"7870">
<li data-start=3D"7616" data-end=3D"7724" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7618" data-end=3D"7724" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
618" data-end=3D"7632">Analogique</strong> : Plus pr=C3=A9cis dans la repr=
=C3=A9sentation des ph=C3=A9nom=C3=A8nes naturels, mais sujet aux interf=C3=
=A9rences.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7725" data-end=3D"7870" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7727" data-end=3D"7870" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
727" data-end=3D"7740">Num=C3=A9rique</strong> : Moins pr=C3=A9cis que les =
signaux analogiques dans la repr=C3=A9sentation continue, mais plus robuste=
 et fiable sur de longues distances.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7872" data-end=3D"7905" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7876" data-end=3D"7905">4.1.3 R=C3=A9silience au Bruit</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7906" data-end=3D"8075">
<li data-start=3D"7906" data-end=3D"7986" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7908" data-end=3D"7986" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
908" data-end=3D"7922">Analogique</strong> : Sensible au bruit et =C3=A0 la=
 distorsion pendant la transmission.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7987" data-end=3D"8075" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7989" data-end=3D"8075" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
989" data-end=3D"8002">Num=C3=A9rique</strong> : Moins sensible au bruit, c=
e qui permet des transmissions plus fiables.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"8077" data-end=3D"8080" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"8082" data-end=3D"8141" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8084" data-end=3D"8141">Chapitre 5 : Applications des Signaux (Niveau Avanc=
=C3=A9)</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"8143" data-end=3D"8190" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8146" data-end=3D"8190">5.1 Applications des Signaux Analogiques</strong></=
h2>
<ul data-start=3D"8191" data-end=3D"8590">
<li data-start=3D"8191" data-end=3D"8265" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8193" data-end=3D"8265" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
193" data-end=3D"8223">Audio et vid=C3=A9o analogiques</strong> : T=C3=A9l=
=C3=A9vision traditionnelle, radio AM/FM.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8266" data-end=3D"8393" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8268" data-end=3D"8393" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
268" data-end=3D"8291">Mesures et capteurs</strong> : Les capteurs de temp=
=C3=A9rature, de pression et d'humidit=C3=A9 produisent des signaux analogi=
ques continus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8394" data-end=3D"8590" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8396" data-end=3D"8590" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
396" data-end=3D"8420">Syst=C3=A8mes de contr=C3=B4le</strong> : Les syst=
=C3=A8mes de contr=C3=B4le industriels utilisent souvent des signaux analog=
iques pour des applications telles que la r=C3=A9gulation de temp=C3=A9ratu=
re, de pression, et de d=C3=A9bit.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start=3D"8592" data-end=3D"8638" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8595" data-end=3D"8638">5.2 Applications des Signaux Num=C3=A9riques</stron=
g></h2>
<ul data-start=3D"8639" data-end=3D"9055">
<li data-start=3D"8639" data-end=3D"8730" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8641" data-end=3D"8730" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
641" data-end=3D"8668">Communication num=C3=A9rique</strong> : Internet, r=
=C3=A9seaux mobiles, communication par fibre optique.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8731" data-end=3D"8876" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8733" data-end=3D"8876" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
733" data-end=3D"8759">Traitement des donn=C3=A9es</strong> : Les ordinateu=
rs, les smartphones, et presque toutes les technologies modernes reposent s=
ur des signaux num=C3=A9riques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8877" data-end=3D"9055" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8879" data-end=3D"9055" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
879" data-end=3D"8902">Stockage de donn=C3=A9es</strong> : Les disques durs=
, les SSD, et les syst=C3=A8mes de stockage en cloud utilisent des signaux =
num=C3=A9riques pour l=E2=80=99enregistrement et la r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9ration =
des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"9057" data-end=3D"9060" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"9062" data-end=3D"9118" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
