258" data-end=3D"2278">Couche Transport</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2279" data-end=3D"2300" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2282" data-end=3D"2300" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
282" data-end=3D"2300">Couche Session</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2301" data-end=3D"2327" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2304" data-end=3D"2327" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
304" data-end=3D"2327">Couche Pr=C3=A9sentation</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2328" data-end=3D"2353" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2331" data-end=3D"2353" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
331" data-end=3D"2353">Couche Application</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2355" data-end=3D"2481" class=3D"">Chacune de ces couches =
a une fonction distincte dans le processus de communication. Voici un aper=
=C3=A7u d=C3=A9taill=C3=A9 de chaque couche.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2483" data-end=3D"2486" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2488" data-end=3D"2542" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2491" data-end=3D"2542">2.1 Couche 1 : Couche Physique (Physical Layer)</st=
rong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2544" data-end=3D"2615" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2548" data-end=3D"2568">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> Transmission des bit=
s sur le support physique.</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2617" data-end=3D"2977" class=3D"">La couche physique est =
la couche la plus basse du mod=C3=A8le OSI et elle est responsable de la tr=
ansmission des <strong data-start=3D"2725" data-end=3D"2733">bits</strong> =
sous forme de signaux =C3=A9lectriques, optiques ou radio, sur le m=C3=A9di=
a physique (c=C3=A2bles, fibres optiques, ondes radio). Elle d=C3=A9finit =
=C3=A9galement les sp=C3=A9cifications mat=C3=A9rielles de l'interface r=C3=
=A9seau, comme les connecteurs, les c=C3=A2bles et les voltages.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"2979" data-end=3D"3035" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2984" data-end=3D"3035">Exemples de Technologies =C3=A0 la Couche Physique =
:</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3036" data-end=3D"3301">
<li data-start=3D"3036" data-end=3D"3130" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3038" data-end=3D"3130" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
038" data-end=3D"3065">C=C3=A2ble Ethernet (Cuivre)</strong> : Utilis=C3=A9=
 dans la transmission des donn=C3=A9es par paires torsad=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3131" data-end=3D"3238" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3133" data-end=3D"3238" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
133" data-end=3D"3150">Fibre Optique</strong> : Utilis=C3=A9e pour des comm=
unications =C3=A0 grande distance et avec une bande passante =C3=A9lev=C3=
=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3239" data-end=3D"3298" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3241" data-end=3D"3298" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
241" data-end=3D"3250">Wi-Fi</strong> : Les ondes radio pour les connexions=
 sans fil.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3302" data-end=3D"3335" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3307" data-end=3D"3335">Exemples de Protocoles :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3336" data-end=3D"3389">
<li data-start=3D"3336" data-end=3D"3363" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3338" data-end=3D"3363" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
338" data-end=3D"3352">IEEE 802.3</strong> (Ethernet)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3364" data-end=3D"3389" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3366" data-end=3D"3389" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
366" data-end=3D"3381">IEEE 802.11</strong> (Wi-Fi)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3391" data-end=3D"3394" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3396" data-end=3D"3461" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3399" data-end=3D"3461">2.2 Couche 2 : Couche Liaison de Donn=C3=A9es (Data=
 Link Layer)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3463" data-end=3D"3581" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3467" data-end=3D"3487">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> Fournir un transfert=
 fiable de donn=C3=A9es entre deux dispositifs sur le m=C3=AAme r=C3=A9seau=
 local (LAN).</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3583" data-end=3D"3872" class=3D"">La couche liaison de do=
nn=C3=A9es a pour r=C3=B4le de pr=C3=A9parer les donn=C3=A9es re=C3=A7ues d=
e la couche physique et de les organiser sous forme de <strong data-start=
=3D"3711" data-end=3D"3721">trames</strong>. Elle assure =C3=A9galement la =
<strong data-start=3D"3748" data-end=3D"3790">d=C3=A9tection et la correcti=
on des erreurs</strong> qui peuvent survenir lors de la transmission, et g=
=C3=A8re l'acc=C3=A8s au m=C3=A9dium physique.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"3874" data-end=3D"3923" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3879" data-end=3D"3923">Exemples de Protocoles et Technologies :</strong></=
h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3924" data-end=3D"4240">
<li data-start=3D"3924" data-end=3D"3995" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3926" data-end=3D"3995" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
926" data-end=3D"3938">Ethernet</strong> : La norme Ethernet qui d=C3=A9fin=
it la structure des trames.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3996" data-end=3D"4076" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3998" data-end=3D"4076" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
998" data-end=3D"4031">PPP (Point-to-Point Protocol)</strong> : Utilis=C3=
=A9 dans les connexions point =C3=A0 point.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4077" data-end=3D"4240" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4079" data-end=3D"4240" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
079" data-end=3D"4109">MAC (Media Access Control)</strong> : Un sous-ensemb=
le de la couche de liaison de donn=C3=A9es, responsable de l'adresse MAC po=
ur identifier les dispositifs sur le r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4242" data-end=3D"4267" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4247" data-end=3D"4267">Fonctions cl=C3=A9s :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4268" data-end=3D"4498">
<li data-start=3D"4268" data-end=3D"4373" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4270" data-end=3D"4373" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
270" data-end=3D"4290">Contr=C3=B4le de flux</strong> : Emp=C3=AAche les r=
=C3=A9cepteurs de recevoir plus de donn=C3=A9es qu'ils ne peuvent en traite=
r.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4374" data-end=3D"4498" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4376" data-end=3D"4498" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
376" data-end=3D"4400">Contr=C3=B4le des erreurs</strong> : Comme les CRC (=
Cyclic Redundancy Check), pour d=C3=A9tecter et corriger les erreurs de tra=
nsmission.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4500" data-end=3D"4503" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4505" data-end=3D"4556" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4508" data-end=3D"4556">2.3 Couche 3 : Couche R=C3=A9seau (Network Layer)</=
strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4558" data-end=3D"4630" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4562" data-end=3D"4582">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> Acheminement des paq=
uets =C3=A0 travers les r=C3=A9seaux.</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4632" data-end=3D"4914" class=3D"">La couche r=C3=A9seau e=
st responsable de l'<strong data-start=3D"4670" data-end=3D"4698">acheminem=
ent des paquets</strong> de donn=C3=A9es entre les h=C3=B4tes de diff=C3=A9=
rents r=C3=A9seaux. Elle g=C3=A8re =C3=A9galement les aspects de <strong da=
ta-start=3D"4784" data-end=3D"4795">routage</strong> (envoi des paquets ver=
s la destination via le meilleur chemin) et de <strong data-start=3D"4865" =
data-end=3D"4882">fragmentation</strong> des paquets lorsque n=C3=A9cessair=
e.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4916" data-end=3D"4948" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4921" data-end=3D"4948">Protocoles Importants :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4949" data-end=3D"5292">
<li data-start=3D"4949" data-end=3D"5101" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4951" data-end=3D"5101" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
951" data-end=3D"4977">IP (Internet Protocol)</strong> : Le protocole princ=
ipal qui d=C3=A9termine l'adresse logique (adresse IP) d'un dispositif et p=
ermet l'acheminement des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5102" data-end=3D"5214" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5104" data-end=3D"5214" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
104" data-end=3D"5148">ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol)</strong> : =
Utilis=C3=A9 pour des messages de contr=C3=B4le r=C3=A9seau (comme les ping=
s).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5215" data-end=3D"5292" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5217" data-end=3D"5292" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
217" data-end=3D"5228">Routage</strong> : Protocoles de routage tels que <s=
trong data-start=3D"5262" data-end=3D"5270">OSPF</strong>, <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"5272" data-end=3D"5279">BGP</strong>, et <strong data-start=3D"5284" =
data-end=3D"5291">RIP</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"5294" data-end=3D"5319" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5299" data-end=3D"5319">Fonctions cl=C3=A9s :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"5320" data-end=3D"5485">
<li data-start=3D"5320" data-end=3D"5410" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5322" data-end=3D"5410" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
322" data-end=3D"5333">Routage</strong> : Dirige les paquets =C3=A0 travers=
 le r=C3=A9seau en utilisant des tables de routage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5411" data-end=3D"5485" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5413" data-end=3D"5485" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
413" data-end=3D"5432">Adresse logique</strong> : Attribution d'une adresse=
 IP pour chaque appareil.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5487" data-end=3D"5490" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5492" data-end=3D"5548" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5495" data-end=3D"5548">2.4 Couche 4 : Couche Transport (Transport Layer)</=
strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5550" data-end=3D"5624" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5554" data-end=3D"5574">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> Assurer une communic=
ation de bout en bout fiable.</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5626" data-end=3D"5951" class=3D"">La couche de transport =
garantit la <strong data-start=3D"5661" data-end=3D"5676">reliabilit=C3=A9<=
/strong> de la communication de bout en bout entre deux syst=C3=A8mes, en o=
rganisant les paquets re=C3=A7us et envoy=C3=A9s. Elle fournit =C3=A9galeme=
nt des m=C3=A9canismes pour <strong data-start=3D"5821" data-end=3D"5848">c=
ontr=C3=B4ler la congestion</strong>, et la <strong data-start=3D"5856" dat=
a-end=3D"5883">r=C3=A9partition des donn=C3=A9es</strong> (c=E2=80=99est-=
=C3=A0-dire d=C3=A9couper les donn=C3=A9es en segments et les r=C3=A9assemb=
ler).</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5953" data-end=3D"5985" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5958" data-end=3D"5985">Protocoles Importants :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"5986" data-end=3D"6282">
<li data-start=3D"5986" data-end=3D"6125" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5988" data-end=3D"6125" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
988" data-end=3D"6027">TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)</strong> : Utili=
s=C3=A9 pour assurer la fiabilit=C3=A9, le contr=C3=B4le de flux et la retr=
ansmission des paquets perdus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6126" data-end=3D"6282" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6128" data-end=3D"6282" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
128" data-end=3D"6160">UDP (User Datagram Protocol)</strong> : Utilis=C3=A9=
 pour des communications rapides sans garantie de fiabilit=C3=A9 (par exemp=
le pour la voix sur IP ou les flux vid=C3=A9o).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"6284" data-end=3D"6309" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6289" data-end=3D"6309">Fonctions cl=C3=A9s :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"6310" data-end=3D"6552">
<li data-start=3D"6310" data-end=3D"6414" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6312" data-end=3D"6414" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
312" data-end=3D"6345">Contr=C3=B4le de flux et d'erreurs</strong> : Assure=
 que les donn=C3=A9es arrivent dans le bon ordre et sans erreurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6415" data-end=3D"6552" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6417" data-end=3D"6552" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
417" data-end=3D"6433">Multiplexage</strong> : Permet =C3=A0 plusieurs appl=
ications d'utiliser une m=C3=AAme connexion r=C3=A9seau via les ports (par =
exemple, port 80 pour HTTP).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6554" data-end=3D"6557" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6559" data-end=3D"6611" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6562" data-end=3D"6611">2.5 Couche 5 : Couche Session (Session Layer)</stro=
ng></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6613" data-end=3D"6693" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6617" data-end=3D"6637">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> G=C3=A9rer les sessi=
ons de communication entre applications.</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6695" data-end=3D"6971" class=3D"">La couche session g=C3=
=A8re les <strong data-start=3D"6722" data-end=3D"6751">sessions de communi=
cation</strong> entre les applications. Elle assure l'<strong data-start=3D=
"6790" data-end=3D"6803">ouverture</strong>, la <strong data-start=3D"6808"=
 data-end=3D"6820">maintien</strong>, et la <strong data-start=3D"6828" dat=
a-end=3D"6841">fermeture</strong> des sessions entre les syst=C3=A8mes. Ell=
e peut =C3=A9galement g=C3=A9rer la synchronisation et les contr=C3=B4les d=
e dialogue entre les dispositifs.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"6973" data-end=3D"7006" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6978" data-end=3D"7006">Exemples de Protocoles :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"7007" data-end=3D"7200">
<li data-start=3D"7007" data-end=3D"7115" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7009" data-end=3D"7115" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
009" data-end=3D"7020">NetBIOS</strong> : Un protocole pour g=C3=A9rer les =
sessions de communication dans des environnements r=C3=A9seau locaux.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7116" data-end=3D"7200" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7118" data-end=3D"7200" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
118" data-end=3D"7149">RPC (Remote Procedure Call)</strong> : Utilis=C3=A9 =
pour invoquer des proc=C3=A9dures =C3=A0 distance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"7202" data-end=3D"7227" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7207" data-end=3D"7227">Fonctions cl=C3=A9s :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"7228" data-end=3D"7439">
<li data-start=3D"7228" data-end=3D"7336" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7230" data-end=3D"7336" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
230" data-end=3D"7256">Contr=C3=B4le de la session</strong> : G=C3=A8re l'o=
uverture et la fermeture de la communication entre deux applications.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7337" data-end=3D"7439" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7339" data-end=3D"7439" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
339" data-end=3D"7368">S=C3=A9curisation des sessions</strong> : Impl=C3=A9=
mente parfois des m=C3=A9canismes pour s=C3=A9curiser les communications.</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7441" data-end=3D"7444" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"7446" data-end=3D"7508" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7449" data-end=3D"7508">2.6 Couche 6 : Couche Pr=C3=A9sentation (Presentati=
on Layer)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7510" data-end=3D"7619" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7514" data-end=3D"7534">R=C3=B4le Principal :</strong> Traduction des donn=
=C3=A9es entre les formats utilis=C3=A9s par les applications et le r=C3=A9=
seau.</h3>
<p data-start=3D"7621" data-end=3D"7862" class=3D"">La couche pr=C3=A9senta=
tion traduit les donn=C3=A9es entre le format utilis=C3=A9 par les applicat=
ions et celui utilis=C3=A9 par les couches inf=C3=A9rieures. Elle peut =C3=
=A9galement g=C3=A9rer le <strong data-start=3D"7784" data-end=3D"7796">cry=
ptage</strong>, la <strong data-start=3D"7801" data-end=3D"7816">compressio=
n</strong>, et la <strong data-start=3D"7824" data-end=3D"7861">conversion =
des formats de donn=C3=A9es</strong>.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"7864" data-end=3D"7897" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7869" data-end=3D"7897">Exemples de Protocoles :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"7898" data-end=3D"8073">
<li data-start=3D"7898" data-end=3D"7977" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7900" data-end=3D"7977" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
900" data-end=3D"7911">SSL/TLS</strong> : Utilis=C3=A9s pour le cryptage de=
s donn=C3=A9es (par exemple dans HTTPS).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7978" data-end=3D"8073" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7980" data-end=3D"8073" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
980" data-end=3D"8000">JPEG, GIF, ASCII</strong> : Formats de donn=C3=A9es =
utilis=C3=A9s pour repr=C3=A9senter des images ou des textes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"8075" data-end=3D"8100" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8080" data-end=3D"8100">Fonctions cl=C3=A9s :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"8101" data-end=3D"8243">
<li data-start=3D"8101" data-end=3D"8176" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8103" data-end=3D"8176" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
103" data-end=3D"8130">Compression des donn=C3=A9es</strong> : R=C3=A9duit =
la taille des donn=C3=A9es =C3=A0 transmettre.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8177" data-end=3D"8243" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8179" data-end=3D"8243" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
