<p data-start=3D"70" data-end=3D"356" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"70" =
data-end=3D"82">Objectif</strong> : Ce tutoriel vous guide dans une explora=
tion d=C3=A9taill=C3=A9e du <strong data-start=3D"142" data-end=3D"170">Dom=
ain Name System (DNS)</strong>, un =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment crucial de l'infrastru=
cture d'Internet. Du niveau d=C3=A9butant au niveau expert, nous aborderons=
 son fonctionnement, sa structure, ses m=C3=A9canismes, et ses applications=
 pratiques.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"358" data-end=3D"361" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"363" data-end=3D"420" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"36=
6" data-end=3D"420">Chapitre 1 : Introduction au DNS (Niveau D=C3=A9butant)=
</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"456" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"42=
6" data-end=3D"456">1.1 Qu'est-ce que le DNS ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"457" data-end=3D"782" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D"=
460" data-end=3D"488">Domain Name System (DNS)</strong> est un syst=C3=A8me=
 essentiel qui permet de r=C3=A9soudre les noms de domaine en adresses IP. =
En d'autres termes, DNS traduit les noms de domaine lisibles par l'homme, c=
omme <strong data-start=3D"653" data-end=3D"671"><a data-start=3D"655" data=
-end=3D"669" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www=
.google.com/">www.google.com</a></strong>, en adresses num=C3=A9riques n=C3=
=A9cessaires pour localiser les serveurs sur Internet (par exemple, <strong=
 data-start=3D"763" data-end=3D"780">172.217.9.142</strong>).</p>
<p data-start=3D"784" data-end=3D"1021" class=3D"">L'un des grands d=C3=A9f=
is d'Internet est que les humains pr=C3=A9f=C3=A8rent se souvenir de noms f=
aciles =C3=A0 lire, tandis que les ordinateurs utilisent des adresses IP po=
ur communiquer entre eux. Le DNS agit comme un annuaire qui relie ces deux =
aspects.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1023" data-end=3D"1058" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1027" data-end=3D"1058">1.2 Pourquoi utiliser DNS ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1059" data-end=3D"1256" class=3D"">Sans DNS, chaque utilis=
ateur d'Internet devrait se souvenir des adresses IP de chaque site web qu'=
il souhaite visiter. Le DNS permet de rendre l'utilisation d'Internet plus =
intuitive et accessible.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1258" data-end=3D"1295" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1262" data-end=3D"1295">1.3 Exemple de Fonctionnement</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1376" class=3D"">Imaginons que vous voul=
ez acc=C3=A9der =C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1351"><a dat=
a-start=3D"1334" data-end=3D"1349" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=
=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.com/">www.example.com</a></strong>. Voici =
ce qui se passe :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1377" data-end=3D"1636">
<li data-start=3D"1377" data-end=3D"1434" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1380" data-end=3D"1434" class=3D"">Vous entrez <strong dat=
a-start=3D"1392" data-end=3D"1411"><a data-start=3D"1394" data-end=3D"1409"=
 rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.com=
/">www.example.com</a></strong> dans votre navigateur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1435" data-end=3D"1515" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1438" data-end=3D"1515" class=3D"">Votre ordinateur interr=
oge un serveur DNS pour obtenir l'adresse IP associ=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1516" data-end=3D"1636" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1519" data-end=3D"1636" class=3D"">Le serveur DNS r=C3=A9p=
ond avec l'adresse IP, et votre navigateur se connecte au serveur correspon=
dant =C3=A0 cette adresse IP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"1638" data-end=3D"1744" class=3D"">Ainsi, DNS permet une n=
avigation fluide et sans que l'utilisateur ait =C3=A0 se soucier des d=C3=
=A9tails techniques.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1746" data-end=3D"1749" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1751" data-end=3D"1828" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1754" data-end=3D"1828">Chapitre 2 : Structure et Fonctionnement du DNS (Ni=
veau Interm=C3=A9diaire)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1830" data-end=3D"1858" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1834" data-end=3D"1858">2.1 Structure de DNS</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1859" data-end=3D"1952" class=3D"">DNS fonctionne comme un=
 syst=C3=A8me hi=C3=A9rarchique et d=C3=A9centralis=C3=A9 avec plusieurs co=
mposants cl=C3=A9s :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"1954" data-end=3D"1984" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1959" data-end=3D"1984">2.1.1 Noms de domaine</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"1985" data-end=3D"2046" class=3D"">Les noms de domaine son=
t organis=C3=A9s sous forme de hi=C3=A9rarchie :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2047" data-end=3D"2323">
<li data-start=3D"2047" data-end=3D"2144" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2049" data-end=3D"2144" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
049" data-end=3D"2061">Niveau 1</strong> : Le nom de domaine de premier niv=
eau (TLD), comme <strong data-start=3D"2113" data-end=3D"2121">.com</strong=
>, <strong data-start=3D"2123" data-end=3D"2131">.org</strong>, ou <strong =
data-start=3D"2136" data-end=3D"2143">.fr</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2145" data-end=3D"2239" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2147" data-end=3D"2239" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
147" data-end=3D"2159">Niveau 2</strong> : Le nom de domaine de second nive=
au, tel que <strong data-start=3D"2206" data-end=3D"2217">example</strong> =
dans <strong data-start=3D"2223" data-end=3D"2238">example.com</strong>.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2240" data-end=3D"2323" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2242" data-end=3D"2323" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
242" data-end=3D"2262">Niveau 3 et plus</strong> : Des sous-domaines, comme=
 <strong data-start=3D"2290" data-end=3D"2297">www</strong> dans <strong da=
ta-start=3D"2303" data-end=3D"2322"><a data-start=3D"2305" data-end=3D"2320=
" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.co=
m/">www.example.com</a></strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"2325" data-end=3D"2352" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2330" data-end=3D"2352">2.1.2 Serveurs DNS</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2353" data-end=3D"2513" class=3D"">Les serveurs DNS sont r=
esponsables de r=C3=A9soudre les requ=C3=AAtes en renvoyant l'adresse IP as=
soci=C3=A9e =C3=A0 un nom de domaine. Il existe diff=C3=A9rents types de se=
rveurs DNS :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2514" data-end=3D"3120">
<li data-start=3D"2514" data-end=3D"2653" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2516" data-end=3D"2653" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
516" data-end=3D"2539">Serveurs DNS racine</strong> : Au sommet de la hi=C3=
=A9rarchie, ces serveurs contiennent des informations sur les serveurs DNS =
de niveau sup=C3=A9rieur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2654" data-end=3D"2791" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2656" data-end=3D"2791" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
656" data-end=3D"2679">Serveurs DNS de TLD</strong> : Ces serveurs contienn=
ent des informations sur les domaines de niveau sup=C3=A9rieur comme <stron=
g data-start=3D"2767" data-end=3D"2775">.com</strong>, <strong data-start=
=3D"2777" data-end=3D"2785">.org</strong>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2792" data-end=3D"2946" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2794" data-end=3D"2946" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
794" data-end=3D"2823">Serveurs DNS autoritaires</strong> : Ces serveurs co=
ntiennent les informations pr=C3=A9cises pour un domaine sp=C3=A9cifique, c=
omme les adresses IP de <strong data-start=3D"2930" data-end=3D"2945">examp=
le.com</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2947" data-end=3D"3120" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2949" data-end=3D"3120" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
949" data-end=3D"2975">Serveurs DNS r=C3=A9cursifs</strong> : Ces serveurs =
sont utilis=C3=A9s par les clients pour effectuer des requ=C3=AAtes DNS. Il=
s cherchent la r=C3=A9ponse pour le client et retournent le r=C3=A9sultat.<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3122" data-end=3D"3151" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3127" data-end=3D"3151">2.1.3 R=C3=A9solution DNS</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3152" data-end=3D"3416" class=3D"">Le processus de r=C3=A9=
solution DNS implique la recherche de l'adresse IP associ=C3=A9e =C3=A0 un =
nom de domaine. Cela peut =C3=AAtre effectu=C3=A9 de mani=C3=A8re r=C3=A9cu=
rsive (le serveur DNS recherche la r=C3=A9ponse) ou it=C3=A9rative (le serv=
eur DNS donne la direction =C3=A0 suivre pour obtenir la r=C3=A9ponse).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3418" data-end=3D"3456" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3422" data-end=3D"3456">2.2 R=C3=A9solution DNS en 4 =C3=A9tapes</strong></=
h3>
<ol data-start=3D"3457" data-end=3D"3942">
<li data-start=3D"3457" data-end=3D"3545" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3460" data-end=3D"3545" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
460" data-end=3D"3486">Interrogation initiale</strong> : Un client envoie u=
ne requ=C3=AAte DNS pour un nom de domaine.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3546" data-end=3D"3659" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3549" data-end=3D"3659" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
549" data-end=3D"3576">Recherche dans le cache</strong> : Si le serveur DNS=
 a d=C3=A9j=C3=A0 la r=C3=A9ponse dans son cache, il la renvoie imm=C3=A9di=
atement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3660" data-end=3D"3853" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3663" data-end=3D"3853" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
663" data-end=3D"3703">Interrogation des serveurs r=C3=A9cursifs</strong> :=
 Si la r=C3=A9ponse n'est pas dans le cache, le serveur DNS envoie des requ=
=C3=AAtes aux serveurs DNS de plus en plus sp=C3=A9cifiques, jusqu'=C3=A0 o=
btenir la r=C3=A9ponse.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3854" data-end=3D"3942" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3857" data-end=3D"3942" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
857" data-end=3D"3875">R=C3=A9ponse finale</strong> : Une fois que la r=C3=
=A9ponse est trouv=C3=A9e, elle est envoy=C3=A9e au client.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"3944" data-end=3D"3947" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3949" data-end=3D"4012" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3952" data-end=3D"4012">Chapitre 3 : Types d'enregistrements DNS (Niveau Av=
anc=C3=A9)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4014" data-end=3D"4054" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4018" data-end=3D"4054">3.1 Enregistrements DNS courants</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4055" data-end=3D"4208" class=3D"">Les enregistrements DNS=
 sont des instructions qui renseignent sur les diff=C3=A9rents services d'u=
n domaine. Voici quelques types d'enregistrements courants :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4210" data-end=3D"4258" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4215" data-end=3D"4258">3.1.1 Enregistrement A (Address Record)</strong></h=
4>
<p data-start=3D"4259" data-end=3D"4342" class=3D"">L'enregistrement <stron=
g data-start=3D"4276" data-end=3D"4281">A</strong> associe un nom de domain=
e =C3=A0 une adresse IP de type <strong data-start=3D"4333" data-end=3D"434=
1">IPv4</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4343" data-end=3D"4382">
<li data-start=3D"4343" data-end=3D"4382" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4345" data-end=3D"4382" class=3D"">Exemple : <strong data-=
start=3D"4355" data-end=3D"4382">example.com =E2=86=92 192.0.2.1</strong></=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4384" data-end=3D"4418" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4389" data-end=3D"4418">3.1.2 Enregistrement AAAA</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"4419" data-end=3D"4487" class=3D"">Semblable =C3=A0 l'enre=
gistrement <strong data-start=3D"4448" data-end=3D"4453">A</strong>, mais p=
our les adresses <strong data-start=3D"4478" data-end=3D"4486">IPv6</strong=
>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4488" data-end=3D"4530">
<li data-start=3D"4488" data-end=3D"4530" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4490" data-end=3D"4530" class=3D"">Exemple : <strong data-=
start=3D"4500" data-end=3D"4530">example.com =E2=86=92 2001:0db8::1</strong=
></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4532" data-end=3D"4584" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4537" data-end=3D"4584">3.1.3 Enregistrement CNAME (Canonical Name)</strong=
></h4>
<p data-start=3D"4585" data-end=3D"4710" class=3D"">L'enregistrement <stron=
g data-start=3D"4602" data-end=3D"4611">CNAME</strong> permet de rediriger =
un nom de domaine vers un autre. C=E2=80=99est souvent utilis=C3=A9 pour le=
s sous-domaines.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4711" data-end=3D"4756">
<li data-start=3D"4711" data-end=3D"4756" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4713" data-end=3D"4756" class=3D"">Exemple : <strong data-=
start=3D"4723" data-end=3D"4756"><a data-start=3D"4725" data-end=3D"4740" r=
el=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.com/"=
>www.example.com</a> =E2=86=92 example.com</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4758" data-end=3D"4806" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4763" data-end=3D"4806">3.1.4 Enregistrement MX (Mail Exchange)</strong></h=
4>
<p data-start=3D"4807" data-end=3D"4935" class=3D"">Les enregistrements <st=
rong data-start=3D"4827" data-end=3D"4833">MX</strong> d=C3=A9finissent les=
 serveurs de messagerie pour un domaine. Ils sont utilis=C3=A9s pour la ges=
tion des emails.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4936" data-end=3D"4982">
<li data-start=3D"4936" data-end=3D"4982" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4938" data-end=3D"4982" class=3D"">Exemple : <strong data-=
start=3D"4948" data-end=3D"4982">example.com =E2=86=92 mail.example.com</st=
rong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4984" data-end=3D"5024" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4989" data-end=3D"5024">3.1.5 Enregistrement TXT (Text)</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5025" data-end=3D"5248" class=3D"">Les enregistrements <st=
rong data-start=3D"5045" data-end=3D"5052">TXT</strong> sont utilis=C3=A9s =
pour stocker des informations texte associ=C3=A9es =C3=A0 un domaine, souve=
nt utilis=C3=A9s pour des v=C3=A9rifications comme <strong data-start=3D"51=
73" data-end=3D"5206">SPF (Sender Policy Framework)</strong> ou <strong dat=
a-start=3D"5210" data-end=3D"5247">DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail)</stron=
g>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5249" data-end=3D"5334">
<li data-start=3D"5249" data-end=3D"5334" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5251" data-end=3D"5334" class=3D"">Exemple : <strong data-=
start=3D"5261" data-end=3D"5334">example.com =E2=86=92 "v=3Dspf1 ip4:192.0.=
2.0/24 include:_spf.example.com ~all"</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5336" data-end=3D"5339" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5341" data-end=3D"5392" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5344" data-end=3D"5392">Chapitre 4 : DNS et S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 (Niveau Expe=
rt)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5394" data-end=3D"5438" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5398" data-end=3D"5438">4.1 Probl=C3=A8mes de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 li=C3=A9s =
=C3=A0 DNS</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5439" data-end=3D"5538" class=3D"">Le DNS, bien que fondam=
ental pour l'Internet, peut =C3=AAtre vuln=C3=A9rable =C3=A0 diverses attaq=
ues, notamment :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5540" data-end=3D"5585" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5545" data-end=3D"5585">4.1.1 DNS Spoofing (Cache Poisoning)</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5586" data-end=3D"5782" class=3D"">L'attaque de <strong da=
ta-start=3D"5599" data-end=3D"5615">spoofing DNS</strong> consiste =C3=A0 e=
nvoyer de fausses informations =C3=A0 un serveur DNS afin qu'il cache des e=
ntr=C3=A9es incorrectes. Cela peut rediriger un utilisateur vers un site we=
b malveillant.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5784" data-end=3D"5824" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5789" data-end=3D"5824">4.1.2 DDoS sur les serveurs DNS</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5825" data-end=3D"6006" class=3D"">Les serveurs DNS sont d=
es cibles communes des attaques par <strong data-start=3D"5884" data-end=3D=
"5924">DDoS (Distributed Denial of Service)</strong>. Ces attaques cherchen=
t =C3=A0 saturer les serveurs DNS pour les rendre inaccessibles.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"6008" data-end=3D"6057" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6013" data-end=3D"6057">4.1.3 Attaques de type Man-in-the-Middle</strong></=
h4>
<p data-start=3D"6058" data-end=3D"6200" class=3D"">Si les communications D=
NS ne sont pas s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9es, un attaquant pourrait intercepter les =
requ=C3=AAtes DNS et r=C3=A9pondre avec de fausses informations.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6202" data-end=3D"6239" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6206" data-end=3D"6239">4.2 Solutions de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 DNS</strong></h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"6240" data-end=3D"6327" class=3D"">Pour s=C3=A9curiser les=
 requ=C3=AAtes DNS, plusieurs protocoles et techniques sont mis en =C5=93uv=
re :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6328" data-end=3D"6869">
<li data-start=3D"6328" data-end=3D"6495" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6330" data-end=3D"6495" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
330" data-end=3D"6366">DNSSEC (DNS Security Extensions)</strong> : DNSSEC p=
ermet d'ajouter des signatures cryptographiques aux r=C3=A9ponses DNS afin =
de v=C3=A9rifier leur int=C3=A9grit=C3=A9 et leur authenticit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6496" data-end=3D"6725" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6498" data-end=3D"6725" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
498" data-end=3D"6522">DNS over HTTPS (DoH)</strong> et <strong data-start=
=3D"6526" data-end=3D"6548">DNS over TLS (DoT)</strong> : Ces protocoles s=
=C3=A9curisent les requ=C3=AAtes DNS en les chiffrant, emp=C3=AAchant ainsi=
 les attaques de type <strong data-start=3D"6649" data-end=3D"6670">Man-in-=
the-Middle</strong> et garantissant la confidentialit=C3=A9 des recherches =
DNS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6726" data-end=3D"6869" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6728" data-end=3D"6869" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
728" data-end=3D"6751">Serveurs DNS priv=C3=A9s</strong> : Utiliser des ser=
veurs DNS priv=C3=A9s ou des services DNS s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9s peut r=C3=A9d=
uire les risques li=C3=A9s aux attaques externes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6871" data-end=3D"6874" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6876" data-end=3D"6941" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6879" data-end=3D"6941">Chapitre 5 : Configurer et D=C3=A9panner le DNS (Ni=
veau Expert)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6943" data-end=3D"6980" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6947" data-end=3D"6980">5.1 Configurer un serveur DNS</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6981" data-end=3D"7046" class=3D"">Voici les =C3=A9tapes g=
=C3=A9n=C3=A9rales pour configurer un serveur DNS local :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"7047" data-end=3D"7693">
<li data-start=3D"7047" data-end=3D"7165" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7050" data-end=3D"7165" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
050" data-end=3D"7079">Installer un logiciel DNS</strong> : Utilisez un log=
iciel comme <strong data-start=3D"7109" data-end=3D"7117">BIND</strong> (Be=
rkeley Internet Name Domain) ou <strong data-start=3D"7153" data-end=3D"716=
4">dnsmasq</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7166" data-end=3D"7280" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7169" data-end=3D"7280" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
169" data-end=3D"7199">Cr=C3=A9er des fichiers de zone</strong> : Ces fichi=
ers contiennent les enregistrements pour les domaines que vous g=C3=A9rez.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7281" data-end=3D"7451" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7284" data-end=3D"7451" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
284" data-end=3D"7324">Configurer les serveurs autoritaires</strong> : Assu=
rez-vous que vos serveurs DNS sont correctement configur=C3=A9s pour r=C3=
=A9pondre aux requ=C3=AAtes pour les domaines de votre r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7452" data-end=3D"7563" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7455" data-end=3D"7563" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
455" data-end=3D"7479">Activer le cache DNS</strong> : La mise en cache des=
 r=C3=A9ponses DNS peut am=C3=A9liorer les performances du serveur DNS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7564" data-end=3D"7693" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7567" data-end=3D"7693" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
567" data-end=3D"7594">Tester la configuration</strong> : Utilisez des outi=
ls comme <strong data-start=3D"7623" data-end=3D"7630">dig</strong> ou <str=
ong data-start=3D"7634" data-end=3D"7646">nslookup</strong> pour tester la =
r=C3=A9solution des noms de domaine.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h4 data-start=3D"7695" data-end=3D"7739" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7700" data-end=3D"7739">5.1.1 Exemple de configuration BIND</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"7740" data-end=3D"7819" class=3D"">Voici un exemple simple=
