g></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1874" data-end=3D"2053" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"1878" data-end=3D"1912">adresse IP (Internet Protocol)</strong> est une=
 s=C3=A9rie de nombres unique qui identifie un p=C3=A9riph=C3=A9rique sur u=
n r=C3=A9seau. Elle permet l=E2=80=99<strong data-start=3D"2004" data-end=
=3D"2020">acheminement</strong> des donn=C3=A9es entre les appareils.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2055" data-end=3D"2064" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2065" data-end=3D"2137">
<li data-start=3D"2065" data-end=3D"2091" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2067" data-end=3D"2091" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
067" data-end=3D"2075">IPv4</strong> : <code data-start=3D"2078" data-end=
=3D"2091">192.168.1.1</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2092" data-end=3D"2137" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2094" data-end=3D"2137" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
094" data-end=3D"2102">IPv6</strong> : <code data-start=3D"2105" data-end=
=3D"2137">2001:0db8:85a3::8a2e:0370:7334</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2188" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2143" data-end=3D"2188">1.2 R=C3=B4le des adresses IP dans les r=C3=A9seaux=
</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2189" data-end=3D"2352" class=3D"">L'adresse IP sert =C3=
=A0 <strong data-start=3D"2209" data-end=3D"2248">identifier et localiser u=
n appareil</strong> sur un r=C3=A9seau. Chaque paquet de donn=C3=A9es conti=
ent une adresse <strong data-start=3D"2310" data-end=3D"2320">source</stron=
g> et une adresse <strong data-start=3D"2336" data-end=3D"2351">destination=
</strong>.</p>
