3848" data-end=3D"3869">3.1 Besoin d=E2=80=99IPv6</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3870" data-end=3D"4009" class=3D"">IPv4 est limit=C3=A9 =
=C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"3888" data-end=3D"3916">4,3 milliards d=E2=80=
=99adresses</strong>. Avec l=E2=80=99explosion d=E2=80=99Internet, IPv6 a =
=C3=A9t=C3=A9 cr=C3=A9=C3=A9 avec <strong data-start=3D"3968" data-end=3D"4=
008">340 sextillions d=E2=80=99adresses possibles</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4011" data-end=3D"4062" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4015" data-end=3D"4062">3.2 Structure et notation des adresses IPv6</strong=
></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4063" data-end=3D"4144" class=3D"">Une adresse IPv6 fait <=
strong data-start=3D"4085" data-end=3D"4097">128 bits</strong>, =C3=A9crite=
 en <strong data-start=3D"4109" data-end=3D"4124">hexad=C3=A9cimal</strong>=
 et s=C3=A9par=C3=A9e par <code data-start=3D"4140" data-end=3D"4143">:</co=
de>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4146" data-end=3D"4188" class=3D"">Exemple : <code data-st=
art=3D"4156" data-end=3D"4188">2001:0db8:85a3::8a2e:0370:7334</code></p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4190" data-end=3D"4223" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4194" data-end=3D"4223">3.3 Types d=E2=80=99adresses IPv6</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4224" data-end=3D"4353">
<li data-start=3D"4224" data-end=3D"4261" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4226" data-end=3D"4261" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
226" data-end=3D"4237">Unicast</strong> : pour un seul appareil</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4262" data-end=3D"4304" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4264" data-end=3D"4304" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
264" data-end=3D"4277">Multicast</strong> : pour plusieurs appareils</p>
</li>
