=C3=A9seaux ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2158" data-end=3D"2192" class=3D"">Le subnetting est essen=
tiel pour :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2193" data-end=3D"2635">
<li data-start=3D"2193" data-end=3D"2331" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2195" data-end=3D"2331" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
195" data-end=3D"2233">=C3=89viter le gaspillage d=E2=80=99adresses IP</str=
ong> : Plut=C3=B4t que d=E2=80=99attribuer un grand r=C3=A9seau =C3=A0 un p=
etit groupe d=E2=80=99appareils, on segmente efficacement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2332" data-end=3D"2447" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2447" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
334" data-end=3D"2370">S=C3=A9parer logiquement des segments</strong> : Par=
 exemple, isoler le service administratif des =C3=A9quipes de d=C3=A9velopp=
ement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2448" data-end=3D"2546" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2450" data-end=3D"2546" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
450" data-end=3D"2479">R=C3=A9duire le trafic inutile</strong> : Moins d=E2=
=80=99h=C3=B4tes par sous-r=C3=A9seau =3D moins de diffusion (broadcasts).<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2547" data-end=3D"2635" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2549" data-end=3D"2635" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
549" data-end=3D"2574">Am=C3=A9liorer la s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> : Un v=
irus ou une attaque reste confin=C3=A9 dans un sous-r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2637" data-end=3D"2680" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2641" data-end=3D"2680">1.3 Notion de masque de sous-r=C3=A9seau</strong></=
h3>
<p data-start=3D"2681" data-end=3D"2780" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"2684" data-end=3D"2709">masque de sous-r=C3=A9seau</strong> permet de d=
=C3=A9finir la partie r=C3=A9seau et la partie h=C3=B4te d=E2=80=99une adre=
sse IP.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2782" data-end=3D"2791" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2792" data-end=3D"2933">
<li data-start=3D"2792" data-end=3D"2821" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2794" data-end=3D"2821" class=3D"">Adresse IP : <code data=
-start=3D"2807" data-end=3D"2821">192.168.1.10</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2822" data-end=3D"2871" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2824" data-end=3D"2871" class=3D"">Masque de sous-r=C3=A9s=
eau : <code data-start=3D"2848" data-end=3D"2863">255.255.255.0</code> (<co=
de data-start=3D"2865" data-end=3D"2870">/24</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2872" data-end=3D"2907" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2874" data-end=3D"2907" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
874" data-end=3D"2891">Partie r=C3=A9seau</strong> : <code data-start=3D"28=
94" data-end=3D"2907">192.168.1.0</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2908" data-end=3D"2933" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2910" data-end=3D"2933" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
910" data-end=3D"2925">Partie h=C3=B4te</strong> : <code data-start=3D"2928=
" data-end=3D"2933">.10</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2935" data-end=3D"2938" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"2940" data-end=3D"2967" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2942" data-end=3D"2967">2. Subnetting en IPv4</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"2969" data-end=3D"3008" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2973" data-end=3D"3008">2.1 Structure des adresses IPv4</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3009" data-end=3D"3184" class=3D"">Une adresse IPv4 est co=
mpos=C3=A9e de <strong data-start=3D"3042" data-end=3D"3053">32 bits</stron=
g>, divis=C3=A9s en <strong data-start=3D"3066" data-end=3D"3078">4 octets<=
/strong> (8 bits chacun).<br data-start=3D"3095" data-end=3D"3098">
Exemple : <code data-start=3D"3108" data-end=3D"3121">192.168.1.1</code> co=
rrespond en binaire =C3=A0 <code data-start=3D"3146" data-end=3D"3183">1100=
0000.10101000.00000001.00000001</code>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3186" data-end=3D"3230" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3190" data-end=3D"3230">2.2 Classes d=E2=80=99adresses et subnetting</stron=
g></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3231" data-end=3D"3290" class=3D"">Historiquement, les adr=
esses =C3=A9taient r=C3=A9parties en classes :</p>
