4092" data-end=3D"4117">3. Subnetting en IPv6</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"4119" data-end=3D"4163" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4123" data-end=3D"4163">3.1 Pourquoi le subnetting en IPv6 ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4164" data-end=3D"4247" class=3D"">IPv6 offre un nombre qu=
asi-infini d=E2=80=99adresses, mais le subnetting reste utile pour :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4248" data-end=3D"4351">
<li data-start=3D"4248" data-end=3D"4283" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4250" data-end=3D"4283" class=3D"">Organiser et structurer=
 le r=C3=A9seau</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4284" data-end=3D"4319" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4286" data-end=3D"4319" class=3D"">S=C3=A9parer des domain=
es fonctionnels</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4320" data-end=3D"4351" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4322" data-end=3D"4351" class=3D"">R=C3=A9duire les tables=
 de routage</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4353" data-end=3D"4394" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4357" data-end=3D"4394">3.2 Notation et sous-r=C3=A9seaux IPv6</strong></h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"4395" data-end=3D"4498" class=3D"">Les adresses IPv6 sont =
divis=C3=A9es en <strong data-start=3D"4430" data-end=3D"4467">blocs de 64 =
bits pour les r=C3=A9seaux</strong> et <strong data-start=3D"4471" data-end=
=3D"4497">64 bits pour les h=C3=B4tes</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4500" data-end=3D"4509" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4632">
<li data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4580" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4512" data-end=3D"4580" class=3D"">Pr=C3=A9fixe <code data=
-start=3D"4520" data-end=3D"4540">2001:db8:abcd::/48</code> peut =C3=AAtre =
divis=C3=A9 en sous-r=C3=A9seaux <code data-start=3D"4574" data-end=3D"4579=
">/64</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4581" data-end=3D"4632" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4583" data-end=3D"4632" class=3D"">Un <code data-start=3D"=
4586" data-end=3D"4591">/64</code> contient <strong data-start=3D"4601" dat=
a-end=3D"4631">18 quintillions d=E2=80=99adresses</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4634" data-end=3D"4637" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"4639" data-end=3D"4681" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4641" data-end=3D"4681">4. Techniques avanc=C3=A9es de subnetting</strong><=
/h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"4683" data-end=3D"4729" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4687" data-end=3D"4729">4.1 VLSM (Variable Length Subnet Mask)</strong></h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"4730" data-end=3D"4846" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"4733" data-end=3D"4741">VLSM</strong> permet d=E2=80=99utiliser des mas=
ques de sous-r=C3=A9seau de tailles diff=C3=A9rentes pour optimiser l=E2=80=
=99espace d=E2=80=99adressage.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4848" data-end=3D"4857" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4858" data-end=3D"4939">
<li data-start=3D"4858" data-end=3D"4898" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4860" data-end=3D"4898" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"486=
0" data-end=3D"4865">/24</code> pour un grand r=C3=A9seau (250 h=C3=B4tes)<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4899" data-end=3D"4939" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4901" data-end=3D"4939" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"490=
1" data-end=3D"4906">/28</code> pour un petit segment (14 h=C3=B4tes)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4941" data-end=3D"4979" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4945" data-end=3D"4979">4.2 Supernetting et agr=C3=A9gation</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4980" data-end=3D"5114" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"4983" data-end=3D"4999">supernetting</strong> regroupe plusieurs sous-r=
=C3=A9seaux en un seul grand r=C3=A9seau pour r=C3=A9duire le nombre d=E2=
=80=99entr=C3=A9es dans la table de routage.</p>
