<ul data-start=3D"3801" data-end=3D"3999">
<li data-start=3D"3801" data-end=3D"3931" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3803" data-end=3D"3931" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"3807" data-end=3D"3827">route par d=C3=A9faut</strong> (<code data-star=
t=3D"3829" data-end=3D"3840">0.0.0.0/0</code>) est utilis=C3=A9e pour envoy=
er les paquets qui ne correspondent =C3=A0 aucune autre route connue.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3932" data-end=3D"3999" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3934" data-end=3D"3999" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"3938" data-end=3D"3958">route sp=C3=A9cifique</strong> indique un chemi=
n pr=C3=A9cis vers un r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4001" data-end=3D"4046" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4005" data-end=3D"4044">2.3 Adresse de passerelle (gateway)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4047" data-end=3D"4141" class=3D"">Une passerelle est l'ad=
resse IP d'un routeur qui sert d'interm=C3=A9diaire entre plusieurs r=C3=A9=
seaux.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4143" data-end=3D"4146" class=3D"">
