<h2 data-start=3D"1963" data-end=3D"2004" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1966" data-end=3D"2002">1. Introduction aux Commutateurs</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2006" data-end=3D"2050" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2010" data-end=3D"2048">1.1 D=C3=A9finition et R=C3=B4le d=E2=80=99un Switc=
h</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2051" data-end=3D"2206" class=3D"">Un switch permet l=E2=
=80=99interconnexion des =C3=A9quipements d=E2=80=99un r=C3=A9seau local et=
 utilise les adresses MAC pour acheminer les trames. Il offre plusieurs ava=
ntages :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2207" data-end=3D"2441">
<li data-start=3D"2207" data-end=3D"2310" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2209" data-end=3D"2310" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
209" data-end=3D"2224">Performance</strong> : r=C3=A9duit la congestion en =
commutant les trames uniquement vers les ports concern=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2311" data-end=3D"2369" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2313" data-end=3D"2369" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
313" data-end=3D"2325">S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> : permet l=E2=80=99isola=
tion du trafic via VLANs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2370" data-end=3D"2441" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2372" data-end=3D"2441" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
372" data-end=3D"2387">Scalabilit=C3=A9</strong> : supporte des centaines d=
e connexions simultan=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2443" data-end=3D"2493" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2447" data-end=3D"2491">1.2 Diff=C3=A9rence entre un Switch et un Hub</stro=
ng></h3>
