<hr data-start=3D"3025" data-end=3D"3028" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3030" data-end=3D"3072" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3033" data-end=3D"3072">1. Introduction aux Services R=C3=A9seau</strong></=
h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3074" data-end=3D"3118" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3078" data-end=3D"3118">1.1 Qu'est-ce qu'un service r=C3=A9seau ?</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"3119" data-end=3D"3384" class=3D"">Un service r=C3=A9seau =
est une fonctionnalit=C3=A9 offerte par un serveur ou un dispositif r=C3=A9=
seau pour r=C3=A9pondre =C3=A0 un besoin sp=C3=A9cifique. Par exemple, l'at=
tribution dynamique d'adresses IP via DHCP, la r=C3=A9solution de noms via =
DNS, ou la communication entre dispositifs via HTTP.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3386" data-end=3D"3449" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3390" data-end=3D"3449">1.2 Importance des services dans un r=C3=A9seau inf=
ormatique</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3450" data-end=3D"3781" class=3D"">Les services r=C3=A9sea=
u sont cruciaux pour la gestion et l=E2=80=99exploitation d=E2=80=99un r=C3=
=A9seau informatique. Sans services de configuration, de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9=
, et de communication, un r=C3=A9seau ne pourrait pas fonctionner de mani=
=C3=A8re optimale. Ces services facilitent l=E2=80=99interconnexion des mac=
hines, la gestion des utilisateurs et la protection des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3783" data-end=3D"3840" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3787" data-end=3D"3840">1.3 Vue d'ensemble des services r=C3=A9seau essenti=
els</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3841" data-end=3D"4018" class=3D"">Certains services sont =
fondamentaux pour toute infrastructure r=C3=A9seau : <strong data-start=3D"=
3912" data-end=3D"3919">DNS</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3921" data-end=
=3D"3929">DHCP</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3931" data-end=3D"3945">HTTP=
/HTTPS</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3947" data-end=3D"3955">SMTP</strong=
>, <strong data-start=3D"3957" data-end=3D"3970">IMAP/POP3</strong>, <stron=
g data-start=3D"3972" data-end=3D"3984">SMB/CIFS</strong>, <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"3986" data-end=3D"3993">NFS</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3995" dat=
a-end=3D"4003">LDAP</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"4005" data-end=3D"4012"=
>VPN</strong>, etc.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4020" data-end=3D"4023" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4025" data-end=3D"4071" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4028" data-end=3D"4071">2. Services de R=C3=A9solution de Noms : DNS</stron=
g></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4073" data-end=3D"4106" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4077" data-end=3D"4106">2.1 Fonctionnement de DNS</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4107" data-end=3D"4258" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"4110" data-end=3D"4117">DNS</strong> est le syst=C3=A8me qui traduit le=
s noms de domaine (par exemple, <a data-start=3D"4179" data-end=3D"4194" re=
l=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.com/">=
www.example.com</a>) en adresses IP afin de localiser les ressources sur un=
 r=C3=A9seau.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4260" data-end=3D"4474">
<li data-start=3D"4260" data-end=3D"4381" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4262" data-end=3D"4381" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
262" data-end=3D"4286">Serveur DNS r=C3=A9cursif</strong> : R=C3=A9sout les=
 demandes de traduction d'un nom de domaine en interrogeant d'autres serveu=
rs DNS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4382" data-end=3D"4474" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4384" data-end=3D"4474" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
384" data-end=3D"4411">Serveur DNS autoritaire</strong> : Contient les info=
rmations d=C3=A9finitives pour un domaine donn=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4476" data-end=3D"4509" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4480" data-end=3D"4509">2.2 Types de serveurs DNS</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4704">
<li data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4608" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4512" data-end=3D"4608" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
512" data-end=3D"4533">Serveur DNS local</strong> : Cache les r=C3=A9ponses=
 des demandes pour am=C3=A9liorer la vitesse de r=C3=A9solution.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4609" data-end=3D"4704" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4611" data-end=3D"4704" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
611" data-end=3D"4637">Serveur DNS secondaire</strong> : Assure la redondan=
ce en cas de d=C3=A9faillance du serveur principal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4706" data-end=3D"4748" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4710" data-end=3D"4748">2.3 Configuration d'un serveur DNS</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4749" data-end=3D"4850" class=3D"">Pour configurer un serv=
eur DNS local avec <strong data-start=3D"4791" data-end=3D"4799">BIND</stro=
ng> (sur un serveur Linux), voici les =C3=A9tapes de base :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"4851" data-end=3D"5011">
<li data-start=3D"4851" data-end=3D"4899" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4854" data-end=3D"4899" class=3D"">Installer BIND : <code =
data-start=3D"4871" data-end=3D"4899">sudo apt-get install bind9</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4900" data-end=3D"4963" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4903" data-end=3D"4963" class=3D"">Configurer le fichier d=
e zone : <code data-start=3D"4935" data-end=3D"4963">/etc/bind/named.conf.l=
ocal</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4964" data-end=3D"5011" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4967" data-end=3D"5011" class=3D"">Cr=C3=A9er un fichier d=
e zone pour votre domaine.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"5013" data-end=3D"5057" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5017" data-end=3D"5057">2.4 D=C3=A9pannage et optimisation du DNS</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"5058" data-end=3D"5200" class=3D"">Utilisez des outils com=
me <code data-start=3D"5084" data-end=3D"5089">dig</code> et <code data-sta=
rt=3D"5093" data-end=3D"5103">nslookup</code> pour tester la r=C3=A9solutio=
n DNS, et configurez le TTL pour r=C3=A9duire la charge sur les serveurs DN=
S.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5202" data-end=3D"5205" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5207" data-end=3D"5259" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5210" data-end=3D"5259">3. Services de Configuration Dynamique : DHCP</stro=
ng></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5261" data-end=3D"5296" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5265" data-end=3D"5296">3.1 Qu'est-ce que le DHCP ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5297" data-end=3D"5508" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"5300" data-end=3D"5308">DHCP</strong> (Dynamic Host Configuration Proto=
col) permet =C3=A0 un serveur d'attribuer automatiquement une adresse IP et=
 d'autres param=C3=A8tres r=C3=A9seau (comme la passerelle et les serveurs =
DNS) aux appareils d'un r=C3=A9seau.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5510" data-end=3D"5544" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5514" data-end=3D"5544">3.2 Fonctionnement du DHCP</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5545" data-end=3D"5685" class=3D"">Lorsqu'un appareil se c=
onnecte au r=C3=A9seau, il envoie une demande DHCP. Le serveur DHCP r=C3=A9=
pond avec les param=C3=A8tres n=C3=A9cessaires =C3=A0 la connexion.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5687" data-end=3D"5730" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5691" data-end=3D"5730">3.3 Configuration d'un serveur DHCP</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5731" data-end=3D"5797" class=3D"">Sur un serveur Linux, v=
ous pouvez configurer <strong data-start=3D"5776" data-end=3D"5795">ISC DHC=
P Server</strong> :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"5798" data-end=3D"5970">
<li data-start=3D"5798" data-end=3D"5866" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5801" data-end=3D"5866" class=3D"">Installez le paquet DHC=
P : <code data-start=3D"5828" data-end=3D"5866">sudo apt-get install isc-dh=
cp-server</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5867" data-end=3D"5970" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5870" data-end=3D"5970" class=3D"">Modifiez le fichier de =
configuration (<code data-start=3D"5908" data-end=3D"5930">/etc/dhcp/dhcpd.=
conf</code>) pour d=C3=A9finir les plages d=E2=80=99adresses IP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"5972" data-end=3D"6035" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5976" data-end=3D"6035">3.4 R=C3=A9servations DHCP et autres configurations=
 avanc=C3=A9es</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6036" data-end=3D"6212">
<li data-start=3D"6036" data-end=3D"6122" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6038" data-end=3D"6122" class=3D"">R=C3=A9servez des adres=
ses IP sp=C3=A9cifiques pour certains appareils via leurs adresses MAC.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6123" data-end=3D"6212" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6125" data-end=3D"6212" class=3D"">Configurez des options =
DHCP pour la configuration des serveurs DNS ou du temps de bail.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6214" data-end=3D"6217" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6219" data-end=3D"6267" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6222" data-end=3D"6267">4. Services de Communication : HTTP/HTTPS</strong><=
/h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6269" data-end=3D"6310" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6273" data-end=3D"6310">4.1 Qu'est-ce que HTTP et HTTPS ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6311" data-end=3D"6527" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"6314" data-end=3D"6322">HTTP</strong> (HyperText Transfer Protocol) est=
 un protocole de communication permettant la navigation sur le web. <strong=
 data-start=3D"6424" data-end=3D"6433">HTTPS</strong> est la version s=C3=
=A9curis=C3=A9e de HTTP, chiffrant les donn=C3=A9es =C3=A9chang=C3=A9es ave=
c un certificat SSL/TLS.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6529" data-end=3D"6581" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6533" data-end=3D"6581">4.2 Fonctionnement des Protocoles HTTP/HTTPS</stron=
g></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6582" data-end=3D"6770" class=3D"">Les protocoles HTTP et =
HTTPS permettent la communication entre un client (comme un navigateur) et =
un serveur web. HTTPS chiffre les donn=C3=A9es pour garantir la confidentia=
lit=C3=A9 et l'int=C3=A9grit=C3=A9.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6772" data-end=3D"6832" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6776" data-end=3D"6832">4.3 Mise en place d'un serveur Web avec Apache/Ngin=
x</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"6833" data-end=3D"7010">
<li data-start=3D"6833" data-end=3D"6885" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6836" data-end=3D"6885" class=3D"">Installez Apache : <cod=
e data-start=3D"6855" data-end=3D"6885">sudo apt-get install apache2</code>=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6886" data-end=3D"6935" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6889" data-end=3D"6935" class=3D"">Testez l'installation a=
vec <code data-start=3D"6916" data-end=3D"6934">http://localhost</code>.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6936" data-end=3D"7010" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6939" data-end=3D"7010" class=3D"">Pour HTTPS, configurez =
SSL avec Let's Encrypt : <code data-start=3D"6987" data-end=3D"7010">sudo c=
ertbot --apache</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"7012" data-end=3D"7015" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"7017" data-end=3D"7062" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7020" data-end=3D"7062">5. Services de Mail : SMTP, IMAP, POP3</strong></h2=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"7064" data-end=3D"7115" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7068" data-end=3D"7115">5.1 Introduction aux services de messagerie</strong=
></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7116" data-end=3D"7323">
<li data-start=3D"7116" data-end=3D"7168" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7118" data-end=3D"7168" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
118" data-end=3D"7126">SMTP</strong> : Protocol utilis=C3=A9 pour l'envoi d=
e mails.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7169" data-end=3D"7250" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7171" data-end=3D"7250" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
171" data-end=3D"7179">IMAP</strong> : Protocol utilis=C3=A9 pour la r=C3=
=A9ception et la gestion des mails en ligne.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7251" data-end=3D"7323" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7253" data-end=3D"7323" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
253" data-end=3D"7261">POP3</strong> : Protocol permettant de t=C3=A9l=C3=
=A9charger les mails sur le client.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7325" data-end=3D"7369" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7329" data-end=3D"7369">5.2 Fonctionnement de chaque service</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"7370" data-end=3D"7504" class=3D"">SMTP sert =C3=A0 envoye=
r des e-mails =C3=A0 un serveur. IMAP et POP3 permettent de r=C3=A9cup=C3=
=A9rer ces e-mails pour les lire localement sur un client.</p>
