<hr data-start=3D"2350" data-end=3D"2353" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2355" data-end=3D"2382" class=3D"">1. Introduction au Wi-=
Fi</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2384" data-end=3D"2420" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2388" data-end=3D"2420">1.1 Qu'est-ce que le Wi-Fi ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2421" data-end=3D"2835" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"2424" data-end=3D"2433">Wi-Fi</strong> (abr=C3=A9viation de "Wireless F=
idelity") est une technologie de r=C3=A9seau sans fil qui permet de connect=
er des appareils comme des ordinateurs, des smartphones, des tablettes, des=
 imprimantes et m=C3=AAme des objets intelligents =C3=A0 un r=C3=A9seau loc=
al (LAN) sans l=E2=80=99utilisation de c=C3=A2bles. Le Wi-Fi fonctionne en =
utilisant des ondes radio pour transmettre les donn=C3=A9es entre les appar=
eils et les points d'acc=C3=A8s au r=C3=A9seau.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2837" data-end=3D"2881" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2841" data-end=3D"2881">1.2 Historique et =C3=A9volution du Wi-Fi</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"2882" data-end=3D"3005" class=3D"">Le Wi-Fi a =C3=A9volu=
=C3=A9 au fil des ann=C3=A9es, avec des am=C3=A9liorations significatives e=
n termes de vitesse, de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 et de port=C3=A9e :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3006" data-end=3D"3389">
<li data-start=3D"3006" data-end=3D"3081" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3008" data-end=3D"3081" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
008" data-end=3D"3016">1997</strong> : Introduction de la norme IEEE 802.11=
, la premi=C3=A8re norme Wi-Fi.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3082" data-end=3D"3141" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3084" data-end=3D"3141" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
084" data-end=3D"3092">2003</strong> : 802.11g, augmentation de la vitesse =
=C3=A0 54 Mbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3142" data-end=3D"3222" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3144" data-end=3D"3222" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
144" data-end=3D"3152">2009</strong> : 802.11n, support de vitesses de 600 =
Mbps et des antennes multiples.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3223" data-end=3D"3285" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3225" data-end=3D"3285" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
225" data-end=3D"3233">2013</strong> : 802.11ac, jusqu'=C3=A0 1,3 Gbps sur =
les r=C3=A9seaux 5 GHz.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3286" data-end=3D"3389" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3288" data-end=3D"3389" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
288" data-end=3D"3296">2019</strong> : 802.11ax (Wi-Fi 6), am=C3=A9lioratio=
n de l'efficacit=C3=A9 du r=C3=A9seau dans des environnements denses.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3391" data-end=3D"3434" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3395" data-end=3D"3434">1.3 Applications courantes du Wi-Fi</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3435" data-end=3D"3728">
<li data-start=3D"3435" data-end=3D"3532" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3437" data-end=3D"3532" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
437" data-end=3D"3456">Dans les foyers</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s =C3=A0 Interne=
t, services de streaming, jeux en ligne, objets connect=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3533" data-end=3D"3636" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3535" data-end=3D"3636" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
535" data-end=3D"3559">Dans les entreprises</strong> : R=C3=A9seaux priv=C3=
=A9s, gestion des p=C3=A9riph=C3=A9riques mobiles, conf=C3=A9rences vid=C3=
=A9o, VPN.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3637" data-end=3D"3728" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3639" data-end=3D"3728" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
639" data-end=3D"3667">Dans les espaces publics</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s =C3=
=A0 Internet dans les caf=C3=A9s, h=C3=B4tels, gares, a=C3=A9roports.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3730" data-end=3D"3733" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3735" data-end=3D"3777" class=3D"">2. Principes de Foncti=
onnement du Wi-Fi</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3779" data-end=3D"3814" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3783" data-end=3D"3814">2.1 Le r=C3=B4le des ondes radio</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3815" data-end=3D"4225" class=3D"">Le Wi-Fi utilise des <s=
trong data-start=3D"3836" data-end=3D"3851">ondes radio</strong> pour trans=
mettre les donn=C3=A9es sans fil. Ces ondes sont envoy=C3=A9es et re=C3=A7u=
es par des antennes dans les points d'acc=C3=A8s (AP) et les appareils clie=
nts. Lorsque vous envoyez une requ=C3=AAte via votre appareil (comme un sma=
rtphone), celui-ci transmet un signal radio =C3=A0 un point d'acc=C3=A8s, q=
ui =C3=A0 son tour relaie cette information vers Internet via un c=C3=A2ble=
 Ethernet ou une connexion fibre.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4227" data-end=3D"4277" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4231" data-end=3D"4277">2.2 Le mod=C3=A8le client-serveur dans le Wi-Fi</st=
rong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4278" data-end=3D"4354" class=3D"">Le r=C3=A9seau Wi-Fi fo=
nctionne g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement selon un mod=C3=A8le <strong data-start=3D"=
4334" data-end=3D"4352">client-serveur</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4355" data-end=3D"4646">
<li data-start=3D"4355" data-end=3D"4464" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4357" data-end=3D"4464" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
357" data-end=3D"4373">Client Wi-Fi</strong> : L'appareil (ordinateur, smar=
tphone, etc.) qui cherche =C3=A0 se connecter au r=C3=A9seau sans fil.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4465" data-end=3D"4646" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4467" data-end=3D"4646" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
467" data-end=3D"4489">Point d'acc=C3=A8s (AP)</strong> : Un p=C3=A9riph=C3=
=A9rique central qui permet la communication entre les clients Wi-Fi et le =
r=C3=A9seau filaire. Il sert d'interface pour acc=C3=A9der =C3=A0 Internet =
ou =C3=A0 un LAN.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4648" data-end=3D"4703" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4652" data-end=3D"4703">2.3 Fr=C3=A9quences et bandes de fr=C3=A9quence uti=
lis=C3=A9es</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4704" data-end=3D"4782" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"4708" data-end=3D"4731">bandes de fr=C3=A9quence</strong> les plus cour=
amment utilis=C3=A9es pour le Wi-Fi sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4783" data-end=3D"5011">
<li data-start=3D"4783" data-end=3D"4918" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4785" data-end=3D"4918" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
785" data-end=3D"4796">2,4 GHz</strong> : Plus longue port=C3=A9e, mais plu=
s susceptible aux interf=C3=A9rences d'autres appareils (microwaves, t=C3=
=A9l=C3=A9phones sans fil, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4919" data-end=3D"5011" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4921" data-end=3D"5011" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
921" data-end=3D"4930">5 GHz</strong> : Plus rapide et moins sujet aux inte=
rf=C3=A9rences, mais la port=C3=A9e est plus limit=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5013" data-end=3D"5063" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5017" data-end=3D"5063">2.4 Modulation et d=C3=A9modulation des signaux</st=
rong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5064" data-end=3D"5209" class=3D"">Le Wi-Fi utilise des te=
chniques de <strong data-start=3D"5099" data-end=3D"5113">modulation</stron=
g> pour encoder les donn=C3=A9es dans les signaux radio. Les deux principau=
x types de modulation sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5210" data-end=3D"5498">
<li data-start=3D"5210" data-end=3D"5398" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5212" data-end=3D"5398" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
212" data-end=3D"5265">OFDM (Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing)</s=
trong> : Utilis=C3=A9 dans les normes modernes (802.11n, 802.11ac, 802.11ax=
), permettant de transmettre plusieurs flux de donn=C3=A9es simultan=C3=A9m=
ent.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5399" data-end=3D"5498" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5401" data-end=3D"5498" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
401" data-end=3D"5443">DSSS (Direct Sequence Spread Spectrum)</strong> : Ut=
ilis=C3=A9 dans les anciennes normes Wi-Fi (802.11b/g).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5500" data-end=3D"5503" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5505" data-end=3D"5539" class=3D"">3. Normes et Technolog=
ies Wi-Fi</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5541" data-end=3D"5603" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5545" data-end=3D"5603">3.1 Les diff=C3=A9rentes normes Wi-Fi (802.11a/b/g/=
n/ac/ax)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5604" data-end=3D"6082">
<li data-start=3D"5604" data-end=3D"5668" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5606" data-end=3D"5668" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
606" data-end=3D"5617">802.11a</strong> : Fonctionne =C3=A0 5 GHz, vitesse =
maximale de 54 Mbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5669" data-end=3D"5735" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5671" data-end=3D"5735" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
671" data-end=3D"5682">802.11b</strong> : Fonctionne =C3=A0 2,4 GHz, vitess=
e maximale de 11 Mbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5736" data-end=3D"5802" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5738" data-end=3D"5802" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
738" data-end=3D"5749">802.11g</strong> : Fonctionne =C3=A0 2,4 GHz, vitess=
e maximale de 54 Mbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5803" data-end=3D"5893" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5805" data-end=3D"5893" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
805" data-end=3D"5816">802.11n</strong> : Utilise les bandes 2,4 GHz et 5 G=
Hz, avec une vitesse de jusqu'=C3=A0 600 Mbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5894" data-end=3D"5948" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5896" data-end=3D"5948" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
896" data-end=3D"5908">802.11ac</strong> : Fonctionne =C3=A0 5 GHz, jusqu'=
=C3=A0 1,3 Gbps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5949" data-end=3D"6082" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5951" data-end=3D"6082" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
951" data-end=3D"5973">802.11ax (Wi-Fi 6)</strong> : Prend en charge jusqu'=
=C3=A0 10 Gbps, meilleure efficacit=C3=A9 dans des environnements denses, p=
lus faible latence.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6084" data-end=3D"6132" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6088" data-end=3D"6132">3.2 Les caract=C3=A9ristiques de chaque norme</stro=
ng></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6133" data-end=3D"6403" class=3D"">Chaque norme Wi-Fi am=
=C3=A9liore les performances par rapport =C3=A0 la pr=C3=A9c=C3=A9dente. Le=
 passage de 802.11a/b =C3=A0 802.11n a permis de doubler la vitesse, tandis=
 que l=E2=80=99introduction de <strong data-start=3D"6302" data-end=3D"6310=
">MIMO</strong> (Multiple Input, Multiple Output) avec 802.11ac a permis de=
 g=C3=A9rer plusieurs flux simultan=C3=A9s.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6405" data-end=3D"6408" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6410" data-end=3D"6460" class=3D"">4. Composants et Archi=
tecture d=E2=80=99un R=C3=A9seau Wi-Fi</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6462" data-end=3D"6493" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6466" data-end=3D"6493">4.1 Points d=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s (AP)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6494" data-end=3D"6790" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"6497" data-end=3D"6514">point d'acc=C3=A8s</strong> est l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9=
ment cl=C3=A9 de tout r=C3=A9seau Wi-Fi. Il sert =C3=A0 relier les clients =
sans fil =C3=A0 un r=C3=A9seau c=C3=A2bl=C3=A9 ou Internet. Il peut =C3=AAt=
re int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9 dans un <strong data-start=3D"6653" data-end=3D"6664">=
routeur</strong> ou =C3=AAtre un appareil autonome. Le point d'acc=C3=A8s =
=C3=A9met des signaux radio dans une zone sp=C3=A9cifique pour cr=C3=A9er u=
n r=C3=A9seau sans fil.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6792" data-end=3D"6818" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6796" data-end=3D"6818">4.2 Routeurs Wi-Fi</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6819" data-end=3D"7143" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"6822" data-end=3D"6839">routeur Wi-Fi</strong> combine plusieurs foncti=
ons : il distribue l'Internet aux appareils et relie le r=C3=A9seau local (=
LAN) =C3=A0 Internet via une connexion ADSL, fibre optique, ou autre. Les r=
outeurs modernes supportent souvent le <strong data-start=3D"7043" data-end=
=3D"7054">Wi-Fi 6</strong>, offrant de meilleures performances et une gesti=
on optimis=C3=A9e des connexions simultan=C3=A9es.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"7145" data-end=3D"7170" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7149" data-end=3D"7170">4.3 Clients Wi-Fi</strong></h3>
